  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe generic ISO wire post (`assets/posts/wire-iso.cps`) now refuses a non-finite wire number by name. This applies to `PARAM WireTaper`, `WirePlane`, `WireAngle`, `WireU` and `WireV` with the value `null`, `nan` or `inf`. After the refusal, the post writes no cut of that section. The refusal is a `message()`, so the app blocks the NC file (`crates/app/src/posting.rs`).\n\n## The real failure\n\nThe issue said that the post writes `UNaN` or `ANaN`. A test shows a different failure. The app writes a non-finite `f64` as JSON `null`, and the stream parser reads `nan` and `inf` as text. The script skipped each such param with no warning. Thus a leaning move with a bad U, or a bad angle word, posted as a plain `G1 X Y` with no refusal. This is a silent wrong cut. A bad V or a bad taper was refused before, but the message named the wrong cause (\"states no taper\").\n\n## Readings\n\n- The red proof, on the test-only commit `a36ced552` with the old script: `a_non_finite_wire_number_is_refused_by_name_and_writes_no_cut` failed at `script_wire_iso.rs:142` with `null: []`. A null WireU gave no warning.\n- On the fix: `script_wire_iso` passed, 13 of 13 tests.\n- App wire suites: `wire_post` 12, `wire_taper` 10, `wire_taper_angle` 5, `wire_4axis` 8, `conformance` 7. All passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 48 steps, 0 failed.\n\n## Pinning test\n\n`crates/post/tests/script_wire_iso.rs`: `a_non_finite_wire_number_is_refused_by_name_and_writes_no_cut`. It covers a good control section, a bad WireU (`null`, `nan`, `inf`), a bad WireV, a bad WireAngle on an angle-word machine, and a bad WireTaper. For each, it asserts the refusal by name and that no move is written.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes. `cargo xtask gate heavy --base origin/main --dry-run` reaches these app heavy lanes: `conformance`, `control_comp`, `post_cycle_feed_spindle`, `probe_no_coolant`, `program_units`, `wear_comp`, `wire_post`. They did not run here. They go to the cut gate. No NC golden changed.\n- No control ran the output.\n\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/3236-wire-iso-finite-words.md`.\n\nChangelog: The generic ISO wire post refuses a wire number (U, V, taper angle, taper, plane) that is not finite by name. Before, it posted a leaning move as a plain G1.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3236\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
